          "content": "B) Make the case for the strongest candidate\n\n**Explanation:** \nChoosing the most qualified candidate generates the greatest overall benefit for the largest number of people. While favoring the CEO's connection might yield personal and localized short-term gains, hiring the superior candidate maximizes team performance, organizational productivity, and the quality of work delivered to clients or customers. Furthermore, upholding a fair, merit-based process preserves workplace morale, trust, and systemic integrity, preventing the widespread dissatisfaction and inefficiency that nepotism invariably causes.",
